# Data-driven integration test for hackathon/house_move, run by tests/integration/test_house_move_hocons.py.
# Format: https://github.com/cognizant-ai-lab/neuro-san/blob/main/docs/test_case_hocon_reference.md
#
# Discovery accuracy for C-20002 (Glasgow to Darlington, two cars). Ground truth, from the customer's synthetic
# transactions in coded_tools/hackathon/house_move/data/transactions.json:
# - providers: Brightwatt Energy, Fibrely Broadband, Clyde Home Cover, Glasgow City Council council tax, TV Licensing,
#   DVLA vehicle tax (two vehicles), Shieldmotor Insurance (two policies), Pawsure Pet Insurance and the Westend Out of
#   School Club. No water bill: in Scotland water is charged with council tax. Clydeside BS is their own mortgage.
# - life facts: a pet (pet insurance, doggy daycare), a school-age child (out-of-school club) and vehicles.
#
# Providers are checked by keyword where the LLM writes the name consistently, and by `gist` where it may change the
# capitalization (ShieldMotor, VoxMobile); inferred facts and anything worded freely are checked by `gist`.
# The test module issues a fresh session for C-20002 into HOUSE_MOVE_TEST_SESSION_C_20002.
{
    "agent": "hackathon/house_move",
    "timeout_in_seconds": 300,
    "success_ratio": "1/1",
    "connections": ["direct"],
    "interactions": [
        {
            "text": "I'm moving house",
            "sly_data": {"session_token": ${HOUSE_MOVE_TEST_SESSION_C_20002}},
            "response": {
                "text": {
                    "keywords": ["Brightwatt", "Fibrely", "Clyde Home Cover", "TV Licen", "DVLA"],
                    "gist": [
                        """The reply names the providers Shieldmotor and Pawsure among the organizations found.
Capitalization and the words after the brand (for example Insurance, Policy or Mobile) do not matter.""",
                        """The reply lists council tax (Glasgow City Council, or council tax in general) among the
organizations the customer pays.""",
                        """The reply says the customer has, or probably has, a pet (for example because they pay for
pet insurance or doggy daycare).""",
                        """The reply says the customer has, or probably has, a child (for example because they pay an
out- of-school club).""",
                        """The reply says the customer has, or probably has, a car or other vehicle (for example from
vehicle tax or car insurance).""",
                    ]
                }
            }
        },
    ]
}
